/*
 * ProcessInChunks
 *
 * Breaks up a potentially long-running tightly looped task into chunks
 * to avoid noticeable UI blocking in the browser.
 *
 * Parameters:
 *		items: array of items to process
 *		process: function that does the actual work on each item in the above array
 *		context: context in which to call process (what "this" should reference inside the function call)
 *		callback: optional function to perform post-processing if necessary
 *
 * Returns:
 *		none
 *
 * Sample usage:
 *		ProcessInChunks(
 *			[item0, item1, ... ],
 *			function (item) { ... },
 *			window,
 *			function (items) { alert(items.length + " items processed successfully!"); }
 *		);
 *
 * This function was originally written by Nicholas C. Zakas and
 * was released under the MIT license, which appears below.
